  "findings": [
    "Native accepts MaxRate below FixedRate and preserves both boost configuration fields. MaxRate=0/CooldownWindowMinutes=0 produced one HTTP 500 with null message; this does not establish a deterministic rejection contract.",
    "Owned anomaly reports triggered a nonnull SamplingBoost; exact algorithm remains service-owned, not inferred from one observation. Unknown boost rules and inconsistent counters retain native per-document behavior.",
    "Only the uniquely named restrictive custom rule was created and deleted; Default was never mutated. No traces or audit resources created. Native statistics have no delete API.",
    "Discriminating second owned rule: omitting SamplingRateBoost in UpdateSamplingRule removes the existing boost configuration; explicit null also yields no boost. MaxRate=0 with positive cooldown is accepted. Positive MaxRate with zero cooldown and empty boost each produced HTTP 500 with null message. Both owned rules were deleted.",
